  "question": {
    "text": "A balloon moving in a straight line passes vertically above two points&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> on a horizontal plane <math><mn>300</mn></math> ft apart. When above <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> it has an altitude of <math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> as seen from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> When above <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> it has an altitude of <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> as seen from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The distance of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> from the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> where it will touch the plane is"
  },
